{
  "title": "77: Al-Mursalat المرسلات",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالْمُرْسَلٰتِ عُرْفًا ۙ‏(1)\nWAL MURSALAATE U’RFAA.\nBy the [angelic] emissaries sent successively,\nفَالْعٰصِفٰتِ عَصْفًا ۙ‏(2)\nFAL-A’ASEFAATE A’SFAA.\nby those who sweep along like gale,\nوَّالنّٰشِرٰتِ نَشْرًا ۙ‏(3)\nWAN NAASHERAATE NASHRAA.\nby those who publish [the Divine messages] far and wide,\nفَالْفٰرِقٰتِ فَرْقًا ۙ‏(4)\nFALFAAREQAATE FARQAA.\nby those who separate [the truth from falsehood] distinctly,\nفَالْمُلْقِيٰتِ ذِكْرًا ۙ‏(5)\nFALMULQEYAATE ZIKRAA.\nby those who inspire [God’s] remembrance,\nعُذْرًا اَوْ نُذْرًا ۙ‏(6)\nU’ZRAN AW NUZRAA.\nas exemption or warning:\nاِنَّمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ لَوَاقِعٌ ؕ‏(7)\nINNAMAA TOO-A’DOONA LA-WAAQE’.\nwhat you are promised will surely befall.\nفَاِذَا النُّجُوْمُ طُمِسَتْۙ‏(8)\nFA-EZAN NOJOOMO TOMESAT.\nWhen the stars are blotted out\nوَ اِذَا السَّمَآءُ فُرِجَتْۙ‏(9)\nWA EZAS SAMAAA-O FOREJAT.\nand the sky is cleft,\nوَاِذَا الْجِبَالُ نُسِفَتْۙ‏(10)\nWA EZAL JEBAALO NOSEFAT.\nwhen the mountains are scattered [like dust]\nوَاِذَا الرُّسُلُ اُقِّتَتْؕ‏(11)\nWA EZAR ROSOLO UQQETAT.\nand time is set for the apostles [to bear witness]\nلِاَىِّ يَوْمٍ اُجِّلَتْؕ‏(12)\nLE-AYYE YAWMIN UJJELAT.\n—for what day has [all] that been set [to occur]?\nلِيَوْمِ الْفَصْلِ‌ۚ‏(13)\nLE-YAWMIL FASL.\nFor the Day of Judgement!\nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا يَوْمُ الْفَصْلِؕ‏(14)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA YAWMUL FASL.\nAnd what will show you what is the Day of Judgement!?\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(15)\nWAYLUN-Y YAWMA-EZIL LIL-MOKAZZEBEEN.\nWoe to the deniers on that day!\nاَلَمْ نُهْلِكِ الْاَوَّلِيْنَؕ‏(16)\nALAM NOHLEKIL AWWALEEN.\nDid We not destroy the former generations,\nثُمَّ نُتْبِعُهُمُ الْاٰخِرِيْنَ‏(17)\nSUMMA NUTBE-O’HOMUL AAKHEREEN.\n[and] then made the latter ones follow them?\nكَذٰلِكَ نَفْعَلُ بِالْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(18)\nKAZAALEKA NAF-A’LO BIL-MUJREMEEN.\nThat is how We deal with the guilty.\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(19)\nWAYLUN-Y YAWMA-EZIL LIL-MOKAZZEBEEN.\nWoe to the deniers on that day!\nاَلَمْ نَخْلُقْكُّمْ مِّنْ مَّآءٍ مَّهِيْنٍۙ‏(20)\nALAM NAKHLUKKUM MIM MAAA-IM MAHEEN.\nHave We not created you from a base fluid,\nفَجَعَلْنٰهُ فِىْ قَرَارٍ مَّكِيْنٍۙ‏(21)\nFA-JA-A’LNAAHO FEE QARAARIM MAKEEN.\n[and] then lodged it in a secure abode\nاِلٰى قَدَرٍ مَّعْلُوْمٍۙ‏(22)\nELAA QADARIM MA’LOOM.\nuntil a known span [of time]?\nفَقَدَرْنَاۖ فَنِعْمَ الْقٰدِرُوْنَ‏(23)\nFA-QADARNAA, FA-NE’MAL QAADEROON.\nThen We determined; and how excellent determiners We are!\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(24)\nWAYLUN-Y YAWMA-EZIL LIL-MOKAZZEBEEN.\nWoe to the deniers on that day!\nاَلَمْ نَجْعَلِ الْاَرْضَ كِفَاتًا ۙ‏(25)\nALAM NAJ-A’LIL ARZA KEFAATAA.\nHave We not made the earth a receptacle\nاَحْيَآءً وَّاَمْوَاتًا ۙ‏(26)\nAHYAAA-ANW WA AMWAATAA.\nfor the living and the dead,\nوَّجَعَلْنَا فِيْهَا رَوَاسِىَ شٰمِخٰتٍ وَّ اَسْقَيْنٰكُمْ مَّآءً فُرَاتًا ؕ‏(27)\nWA JA-A’LNAA FEEHAA RAWAASEYA SHAAMEKHAATINW WA ASQAYNAAKUM MAAA-AN FORAATAA.\nand set in it lofty [and] firm mountains, and given you agreeable water to drink?\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(28)\nWAYLUN-Y YAWMA-EZIL LIL-MOKAZZEBEEN.\nWoe to the deniers on that day!\nاِنْطَلِقُوْۤا اِلٰى مَا كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(29)\nINTALEQOO ELAA MAA KUNTUM BEHI TOKAZZEBOON.\n[The faithless will be told:] ‘Proceed toward what you used to deny!\nاِنْطَلِقُوْۤا اِلٰى ظِلٍّ ذِىْ ثَلٰثِ شُعَبٍۙ‏(30)\nINTALEQOO ELAA ZILLIN ZEE SALAASE SHO-A’B.\nProceed toward the triple-forked shadow,\nلَّا ظَلِيْلٍ وَّلَا يُغْنِىْ مِنَ اللَّهَبِؕ‏(31)\nLAA ZALEELINW WA LAA YUGHNEE MENAL LAHAB.\nneither shady nor of any avail against the flames.\nاِنَّهَا تَرْمِىْ بِشَرَرٍ كَالْقَصْرِ‌ۚ‏(32)\nINNAHAA TARMEE BE-SHARARIN KAL-QASR.\nIndeed it throws up [giant] sparks like castles,\nكَاَنَّهٗ جِمٰلَتٌ صُفْرٌ ؕ‏(33)\nKA-ANNAHU JEMAALATUN SUFR.\n[bright] like yellow camels.\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(34)\nWAYLUN-Y YAWMA-EZIL LIL-MOKAZZEBEEN.\nWoe to the deniers on that day!\nهٰذَا يَوْمُ لَا يَنْطِقُوْنَۙ‏(35)\nHAAZAA YAWMO LAA YANTEQOON.\nThis is a day wherein they will not speak,\nوَلَا يُؤْذَنُ لَهُمْ فَيَعْتَذِرُوْنَ‏(36)\nWA LAA YOAZANO LAHUM FA-YA’TAZEROON.\nnor will they be permitted to offer excuses.\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(37)\nWAYLUN-Y YAWMA-EZIL LIL-MOKAZZEBEEN.\nWoe to the deniers on that day!\nهٰذَا يَوْمُ الْفَصْلِ‌ۚ جَمَعْنٰكُمْ وَالْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(38)\nHAAZAA YAWMUL FASL, JAMA’NAAKUM WAL AWWALEEN.\n‘This is the Day of Judgement. We have brought you together with the former generations.\nفَاِنْ كَانَ لَكُمْ كَيْدٌ فَكِيْدُوْنِ‏(39)\nFA-IN KAANA LAKUM KAYDUN FA-KEEDOON.\nIf you have any stratagems [left], try them out against Me!’\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(40)\nWAYLUN-Y YAWMA-EZIL LIL-MOKAZZEBEEN.\nWoe to the deniers on that day!\nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ ظِلٰلٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(41)\nINNAL MUTTAQEENA FEE ZELAALINW WA O’YOON.\nIndeed the Godwary will be amid shades and springs\nوَّفَوَاكِهَ مِمَّا يَشْتَهُوْنَؕ‏(42)\nWA FAWAAKEHA MIMMAA YASHTAHOON.\nand [enjoying] such fruits as they desire.\nكُلُوْا وَاشْرَبُوْا هَنِيْٓئًا ۢ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(43)\nKOLOO WASH RABOO HANEE-AM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\n[They will be told:] ‘Enjoy your food and drink, [a reward] for what you used to do.\nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(44)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nThus do We reward the virtuous.’\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(45)\nWAYLUN-Y YAWMA-EZIL LIL-MOKAZZEBEEN.\nWoe to the deniers on that day!\nكُلُوْا وَتَمَتَّعُوْا قَلِيْلًا اِنَّكُمْ مُّجْرِمُوْنَ‏(46)\nKOLOO WA TAMATTA-O’O QALEELAN INNAKUM MUJREMOON.\n‘Eat and enjoy a little! You are indeed guilty.’\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(47)\nWAYLUN-Y YAWMA-EZIL LIL-MOKAZZEBEEN.\nWoe to the deniers on that day!\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمُ ارْكَعُوْا لَا يَرْكَعُوْنَ‏(48)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHOMUR KA-O’O LAA YARKA-O’ON.\nWhen they are told, ‘Bow down [in prayer],’ they do not bow down!\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(49)\nWAYLUN-Y YAWMA-EZIL LIL-MOKAZZEBEEN.\nWoe to the deniers on that day!\nفَبِاَىِّ حَدِيْثٍۢ بَعْدَهٗ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(50)\nFABE-AYYE HADEESIM BA’DAHU YOAMENOON.\nSo what discourse will they believe after this?",
  "merits": "Surah al-Mursalaat (The Emissaries)\nThis is a ‘Makki’ Surah and it has 50 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the one who recites this Surah will not be counted from the polytheists. He will always be victorious over his enemy.\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that drinking this Surah after it is written, and then dissolved in water that is mixed with the water from an onion, acts as a cure from aches and pains. Keeping this Surah, written on deerskin, as a talisman, enables one to reduce the amount of time he sleeps and he will be able to stay awake for a longer time."
}
